WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.560
Well, I came back the Monday after the storm [Hurricane Katrina].

2
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:12.520
One week after the storm I came back, which is very early by most people's return date.

3
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:17.120
My husband, you know, he's a physician, like I said, at EJ [East Jefferson General Hospital].

4
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:26.120
So he had to come back because he knew the people who were there had been there a whole week under horrible conditions and had other things that they had to do.

5
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:32.260
So we came back and we stayed at EJ for a few days in a little . . . on a gurney.

6
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.760
There were no children or elderly in the city when we came back, it was very strange.

7
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:45.180
Go to [New Orleans] City Hall, the staff there is reduced to like a minimum when they need it more than ever.

8
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:52.280
They're working like with a skeleton crew with like this primitive system of musical chairs you know.

9
00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.600
If one person goes in, everybody stands up and moves one chair over.

10
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:01.460
I don't know, I'm not expecting any high tech system but it's like super primitive.

11
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.320
But every time we go, I take my mom,

12
00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:14.900
and we actually always have a good time because we're with like forty, you know, or so people in the same boat.

13
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.820
And people have their pictures with them because it's required for almost everything.

14
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:28.720
And everybody is showing each other their pictures of how nice their . . . Or they're showing the ugly pictures and telling each other how nice their house used to be.

15
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:40.680
It's very therapeutic and it's very interesting because . . . Because of you having to move chairs and it's like you get a new mix of people every twenty minutes.

16
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.920
It's been hilarious, you know, by the time you leave,

17
00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:53.600
you're going to wish people well and it's been kind of fun but not the bureaucracy itself,

18
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.000
but the people that are, like, going through it too.

19
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.500
It's been very bonding.

20
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.580
It's hard to explain.

21
00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:12.100
But to see my mom talking, with the people like that, it's just precious. [laughs] She's encouraging them.

22
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.260
It's you know, I don't know.

23
00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.100
It's just very cute.
